### Setup — Product for billing tests
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "code": "billing-test-product",
  "name": "Billing Test Product"
}

### Setup — Plan (no trial, so the subscription starts ACTIVE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "productCode": "billing-test-product",
  "code": "billing-test-plan",
  "name": "Billing Test Plan",
  "intervalUnit": "MONTH",
  "amountCents": 2999,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Setup — priced entitlement: usage prices live in plan_entitlement's
### jsonb. This meter includes 100 free units, then bills 5 cents each.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/billing-test-plan/entitlements
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "key": "api.calls",
  "value": {
    "includedQuantity": 100,
    "unitAmountCents": 5
  }
}

### Setup — Customer, capture id for use below
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "email": "billing-test@acme.test",
  "name": "Billing Test Customer"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("billingCustomerId", response.body.id);
%}

### Setup — Subscription, capture id for use below
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "customerId": "{{billingCustomerId}}",
  "planCode": "billing-test-plan"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("billingSubId", response.body.id);
%}

### Setup — record usage above the included quantity (100 included,
### 150 recorded -> 50 billable at 5 cents = 250 cents)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{billingSubId}}/usage
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "meterKey": "api.calls",
  "amount": 150
}


### Generate invoice — before the period closes (expects 409 INVOICE_PERIOD_NOT_CLOSED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{billingSubId}}/invoices
X-Tenant-Id: acme


### --- There is no HTTP endpoint to close a billing period early: it
### closes naturally when current_period_end passes, or BillingCycleJob
### rolls it forward on its hourly cron. To exercise the requests below
### without waiting a month, force the period closed in psql first:
###
###   UPDATE subscription SET current_period_end = now() - interval '1 day'
###   WHERE id = '<{{billingSubId}} resolved to its actual value>';
###
### Only then will the requests below return 201 instead of 409.


### Generate invoice — after the period closes (expects 201, BASE + USAGE lines,
### totalCents = 2999 + 250 = 3249). Capture id for use below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{billingSubId}}/invoices
X-Tenant-Id: acme

> {%
    client.global.set("billingInvoiceId", response.body.id);
%}

### Generate invoice — again for the same period (expects 409 INVOICE_ALREADY_EXISTS)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{billingSubId}}/invoices
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Generate invoice — unknown subscription id (expects 404 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_FOUND)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/invoices
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Generate invoice — tenant isolation: acme's subscription id under demo
### (expects 404 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_FOUND — must not leak or succeed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{billingSubId}}/invoices
X-Tenant-Id: demo


### Get invoice by id — expects 200 with BASE and USAGE lines
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Get invoice by id — tenant isolation check (expects 404 INVOICE_NOT_FOUND)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}
X-Tenant-Id: demo

### List invoices for the subscription — expects one invoice
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices?subscriptionId={{billingSubId}}
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### List invoices for the subscription — tenant isolation check (expects empty content)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices?subscriptionId={{billingSubId}}
X-Tenant-Id: demo

### List all invoices for the tenant
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices
X-Tenant-Id: acme
